<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Stocks to Watch Today - April 2.</title>
<headline>Australian Stocks to Watch Today - April 2.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* Mayne Nickless Ltd A$7.85 (-0.27)</p>
<p>Mayne Nickless Ltd said on Tuesday it had made no formal bid for European hospital operator Generale de Sante, despite media speculation to the contrary.</p>
<p>* Westfield Trust A$2.35 (-0.04)</p>
<p>Westfield Trust said late on Tuesday it would buy the remaining 50-percent interest in Melbourne's Doncaster Shoppingtown from National Mutual Holdings Ltd for A$147 million. Westfield would simultaneously sell its 50-percent in West Lakes Shoppingtown in Adelaide to National Mutual for $68 million. Westfield Trust will fund the A$79 million due to National Mutual by additional borrowings.</p>
<p>* Cortecs International Ltd A$5.20 (-0.43)</p>
<p>Cortecs announced on Tuesday its researchers had found a group of novel natural molecules that had anti-cancer properties.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
